WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:05.990
Infinite Ryvius

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.670
Bring the Vital Guarder to a halt!

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.230
Pinger reacting!
We've caught up with the enemy!

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.410
- We're within effective shooting range!
- No, there's too much distance!

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.400
The enemy ship is the
same type as the Ryvius!

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.370
- Yuki! Can you do it?
- Of course.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.350
Then get 'em with one shot.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:23.250
We'll show off our abilities
to those aboard the Ryvius!

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.750
I'll fire one immediately after the other.
I'll sink it with the second shot!

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.520
Opening launch pad!

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.120
- Pinger reacting!
- This is too easy!

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.460
- Finished loading!
- This'll finish you!

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.800
The enemy's course has
been altered by 60 degrees!

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.270
It's a direct hit!

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:47.640
The pinger reaction
has changed to random.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:49.980
The enemy seems to be shredded to pieces.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.420
This should make it clear to you all!

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.410
<i>You guys have no way of surviving</i>
<i>without the Vital Guarder.</i>

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.190
<i>But rest assured.</i>

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.310
<i>We will be your shield,</i>
<i>and protect you.</i>

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.690
<i>In return, don't cause any problems!</i>

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.260
<i>All you have to do is remain</i>
<i>quiet for the next twenty days...</i>

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.490
<i>... until we arrive at Uranus.</i>

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:07.800
<i>Twenty days.</i>

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.460
<i>You only have to put up with</i>
<i>this for twenty days! Got that?</i>

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.770
You're supreme. <i>Ikumi Oze.</i>

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:19.710
<i>How do you manage to be so noble?</i>

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:24.210
Infinite Ryvius

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:31.750
If you're going to walk, right here will be fine

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.760
Although loneliness...

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.090
...can sometimes be unbearable

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:47.330
There's the benefit of not hurting anyone...

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:52.410
...and the benefit of not being exposed...

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:55.380
...and hurt by others as well

00:01:55.880 --> 00:02:02.910
At the opposite side of the frozen sea...

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.690
...the dream and the reality...

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:10.320
...that you saw cross paths

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:14.020
Some light is shed...

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.600
...but how it is done is unknown...

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:25.840
...so that we can go to a different place

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:33.840
The things I want have no shape

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:42.250
Tear the final universe, today until tomorrow

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:56.470
Torn Past

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.910
I'm telling you Guardians
just one more time.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.240
Do not resort to the
excessive use of force.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.270
However, do not overlook anyone
corrupting public morals!

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.240
We will arrive in the vicinity
of Uranus in twenty days.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.550
Until then, we shall become
the law of the Ryvius!

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:14.080
- Right.
- We know, Ikumi.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:19.380
Ikumi Oze. Yuki Aiba.
It's almost time for our meeting.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.720
Yeah. Michelle, look after the rest.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:23.490
I'll do my best, sir!

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:30.840
<i>Ikumi Oze. You are Ritos,</i>
<i>the god of war who protects Mother Arne.</i>

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.570
<i>The one who builds our future.</i>

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.910
<i>Yes... also the future of Kouji and I.</i>

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.410
Are you sure you should be here?

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:46.310
It's not as if I'm neglecting my duties,
so it should be okay.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.890
I've also submitted a
request to be transferred.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:53.490
I'm happy that you're showing
concern for me, but...!

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.100
I'm doing this on my own,
so don't worry.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:57.830
What about Yuki?

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:01.190
Yeah. I worry about him in my own way...

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:03.470
...and I do intend to see him and talk.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.570
But right now, it's you I'm
most worried about, Aoi!

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.670
It's you.

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:14.710
Wow. That sounded like
a declaration of love.

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.780
Not "like", it is.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.620
Sorry... But I...!

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:21.350
Never mind.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.760
It would be great to see Kozue again,
wouldn't it? And Reiko...!

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:34.460
- Get changed here!
- Make sure you never do it again!

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:39.100
Phew! They stuck me in here all day
just because I overslept a bit!

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:41.410
Damn it! Damn you, Ikumi!

00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:43.410
That type of language
won't get you anywhere!

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.070
Why not? He's a friend!

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.880
Assign rooms according to ability?

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:50.510
Yes. Having people of different
abilities live together...

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:52.910
...makes it that much easier for
problems and incidents to arise.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:55.880
I agree. All the fools should
flock together as a group.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.720
Where is there the need to manage
their lives to that extent?

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:00.920
Besides, the incidents
we're having are very minor.

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:03.560
But it's those minor
incidents that, when ignored...

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:05.100
...balloon into major problems
of limitless proportions!

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.030
But...!

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.470
Then what do YOU suggest?

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.140
If you have a better alternative,
then tell us!

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:10.500
Well...!

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.700
Arguing without even an
alternative to suggest?

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:17.680
It's types like you that we need least
on the Ryvius! Get outta here! Now!

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:22.480
You're right.
I may be the one that's mistaken.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:25.950
But at the same time, I can't agree
with your way of thinking either.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:30.250
Ikumi, will you prove to me that
your method is the proper way?

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:32.190
Yeah. I'll prove it to you.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:36.490
All right. Then there's nothing
more that I can do here. Bye.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.000
W-Wait, Juli.

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:42.590
Sorry. But I couldn't
come up with a better way.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:48.540
Give me your word that
Titania will take us in.

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:52.110
That if we endure this situation
for twenty days, we will be saved.

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.050
Yes. I guarantee it.

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:56.920
Thank you. Goodbye.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:04.750
That girl totally irritates me!
She's just like that bastard!

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:08.290
She's very talented, but is easily
swayed by the circumstances.

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:11.490
- With our current system...!
- You don't have to spell it all out.

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:13.600
I'll leave you in charge
of all system changes.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:17.370
- Thank you. I'll do my best.
- Thanks!

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:21.640
What are the ranks of
Kouji Aiba and Aoi Housen?

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.200
Their ranks according to ability.

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:30.510
Oh. I believe they'll both be classified
in C-Class, the average. Why do you ask?

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.680
No reason.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.180
<i>Kouji Aiba.</i>

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:40.430
<i>Your presence appears to rock the faith</i>
<i>in the system shown by those two.</i>

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:44.290
<i>And Juli Bahana.</i>

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:46.700
<i>You as well.</i>

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:49.420
Why did you allocate a child
the lowest ranking E-Class?

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:51.740
- Child?
- I'm talking about Pat Campbell!

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:56.470
The child is of no help to us in the current
situation. I believe it's the proper decision.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:06:59.510
How could you give a ranking to a child?
Provide him with proper care!

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:04.140
I refuse. Ikumi Oze has put me in
charge of this, so that's final.

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.050
Why does that particularly bother you?

00:07:07.450 --> 00:07:09.320
Do you by chance have special
feelings for the child?

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.290
Quibbler!

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.430
Kreis, get the Guardians for me.

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:21.700
Bastard!

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:25.160
The action you have taken severely
disrupts order aboard the Ryvius.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.010
Am I wrong?

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:31.510
Hey, did you see the terminal?

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:34.080
We're assigned to different living
quarters depending on our abilities.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:36.120
How could they make us
move at a time like this?

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:37.980
They're doing whatever they wish!

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:42.480
Charlotte, great news! I've changed
my ranking to E-Class to be with you!

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:46.330
I'm also in the lowest ranked
class all because of you.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:48.250
It's only for twenty days.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.420
Don't you feel guilty?

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:55.030
I've been assigned to the lowest class.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:57.160
Then that makes two of us.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:58.900
What? You too, Aoi?

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.370
I guess I've been too lazy lately.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:03.610
So be it.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:07.770
I understand that this area is for the
lowest class, so we won't have to move.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:10.080
I want you outta here!

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:11.950
Sorry...!

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:13.290
What? What's wrong?

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:15.550
Oh, Kouji. Aoi.

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:19.020
Sorry, but I've been assigned
to B-Class, so I've got to go.

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:21.900
- And Nicks?
- He says he's E-Class.

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:23.800
Don't you mind being separated?

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:26.130
We'd better do as we're told.

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:29.930
I warned Nicks a number of
times not to slack off at work.

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:32.100
Thanks for everything.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:38.330
Goodbye. Watch out for Nicks for me.

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:42.310
Do as you wish. Damn it!

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:51.290
- Our new friends are arriving.
- Yeah. Huh?

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:53.660
You're in here too!

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:55.260
There you go!

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:02.130
They're rotten!
Every one of them controlling the Ryvius!

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:05.970
Pat. Moving once in a
while isn't a bad thing!

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:07.640
Let's cooperate to get through this...

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:10.470
...the worst situation,
until we arrive at Uranus.

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:12.770
I'm all right by myself.

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:14.540
Is that so?

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:17.510
Juli!

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:20.380
Pat! Haven't seen you in awhile.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:22.620
Juli. What are <i>you</i> doing here?

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.450
I was ordered to come here.

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:26.460
Juli. What about the bridge?

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.480
Kouji, you're here too?

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:32.000
What's that noise?

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.670
- An earthquake?
- This is outer space!

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:36.930
- Those partitions!
- They're closing!

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:47.880
The partitions have come down!

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:49.280
- Why?
- What's going on?

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.350
- We might have just been shut in.
- You're kidding...!

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:56.360
The lights!

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.850
Ikumi, that bastard!

00:10:01.390 --> 00:10:04.160
- Ikumi wouldn't do such a thing.
- But he's doing it!

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:08.000
- But...!
- Yuki's on the other side. Why?

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:09.700
The lights have gone out.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.640
Charlie, I'm scared!

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.700
- That voice.
- Is it Charlie?

00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:15.440
Th-They've found us!

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:18.310
I-I beg you. Please forgive us!

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:34.590
Infinite Ryvius

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:39.430
Infinite Ryvius

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:42.360
Is that right. You've been hiding,
within the ship.

00:10:42.770 --> 00:10:44.400
Are you gonna report us to the bridge?

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:48.470
Why should I do anything like that?
I'm no longer Captain of the Ryvius.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:51.070
- Is that so?
- It's a long story.

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:55.410
Yes. Right now, Ikumi Oze
is in control of the Ryvius!

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:59.480
We're completely locked in!

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:01.780
Is there no way outta here?

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.950
No. Every one of the
partitions has been lowered.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:06.250
None of the container routes
are accessible either.

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:09.130
Really. So we're blocked
off in all directions.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:11.030
Boy, I'm starving!

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:14.100
There's no way I'm gonna die of
starvation in a place like this!

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.470
Me neither!

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:18.500
I wouldn't mind as long as I'm with you.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:21.700
What's wrong with you guys? You can't
let something like this keep you down!

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:25.110
It's important to remain cheerful
and joyful under any situation!

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.680
Right Lucson! You said it, right on!

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:31.580
Juli!

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:33.580
We've got lots of food!

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:37.420
Pat! You mustn't bring that out
without consulting with me first!

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:40.420
This is the food that I
gathered in case of emergency...!

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:44.450
My keen foresight had predicted
that this would happen...

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:47.960
...so I stashed away a stockpile of food!

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:50.340
Now, everyone, help yourselves.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:52.970
Eating will do wonders
when you're feeling down!

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:55.000
Thank you, Lucson.

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:59.570
Hey, I'm gonna check around some
more to see if I can find a way out.

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:01.910
- It's dark, so watch out.
- Yeah.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:20.900
Did you find out where Blue is?

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:23.930
Sorry, but there's been
no report on him at all.

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:25.530
Oh.

00:12:43.260 --> 00:12:44.720
Why, you're...!

00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:47.190
Kouji... Aiba...!

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:49.960
You're Neya, right?

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.490
So you're in this Class too.

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:53.860
Couldn't be worse, could it?
For either of us.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.000
Are you all right with this?

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:58.100
As it is?

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:02.000
Of course not!
There's no way this could be "all right"!

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:04.780
What do you want to do?

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:06.540
Well...!

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:14.220
Why all of a sudden?

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:16.420
Did you do something?

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:21.390
I'm amazed you had something like this.

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:23.420
My roommate forgot to take
some things with her.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:26.830
She had a whole range of
crime prevention stuff.

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:29.040
This is like a party!

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:30.440
Our lives are in danger!

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:33.340
By the way, it's almost
Christmas, isn't it?

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:34.640
Today's still the 13th.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:37.510
What's the matter?

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:40.240
December 13th! Today's my birthday!

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:42.180
Really?

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:44.010
Then we'd better celebrate!

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:46.020
Let's do it!

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:50.950
I thought it would lift everyone's... spirit.
Yeah, we should do it.

00:13:52.360 --> 00:13:53.520
<i>What do you want to do?</i>

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:56.230
<i>That's obvious. I!</i>

00:13:56.930 --> 00:13:58.400
<i>I!</i>

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:02.360
<i>Why, this is!</i>

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:10.230
- Kouji.
- What are you doing here?

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:14.040
Tell me how you feel?

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:19.510
What you really want to do. Tell me.

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:24.020
- Pinger reacting!
- An enemy?

00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:25.530
No. Something's strange.

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:27.690
The Geduld's gone in just one area.

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:30.060
In Sere 7?

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:32.030
There's no mistake. And it's huge.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:34.630
There's ordinary space
within the Geduld?

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:37.700
It could be an enemy.
Get Ikumi and Yuki!

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:41.830
Right away. Ikumi,
please answer me. Ikumi!

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.240
<i>Ikumi... Yuki!</i>

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:47.610
<i>Why in the hell are you here?</i>

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:50.910
<i>Kouji. Long time no see.</i>
<i>But we have little time.</i>

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:52.980
<i>If you have something to talk</i>
<i>to me about, make it quick.</i>

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:54.790
What's wrong? Did you reach Ikumi?

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:57.480
Sorry. He seems to be offline.

00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.930
I'll go and look for him.

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:03.950
Ikumi. Tell me.
Why did you lock us up?

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:05.930
Lock you up?

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:07.700
The section we're in.

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.530
The partitions are down,
and none of the lights will turn on!

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:10.700
Heiger!

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:13.830
I'm terribly sorry.
The system appears to be unstable.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:15.780
I'll see that it's taken care of immediately.

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:17.400
If you're done, return to your post.

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.050
I'm not done.

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:20.550
I want you to put a stop to
this crazy system at once.

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:23.340
All it is, is people taking away
the freedom of other people!

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:25.690
- How trivial!
- Yuki!

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:27.290
It's not as small a problem
as you wish to believe!

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:28.790
Who are you to speak?

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:30.660
We're doing it to protect everyone.

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:32.630
It's only for twenty days,
until we get to Titania.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:34.930
I ask that you look the other way sometimes,
for the good of us all.

00:15:34.930 --> 00:15:36.330
We can't wait that long.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:39.530
People are already beginning to go crazy.
Aoi was also close to being assaulted.

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:41.860
- What?
- Aoi? By whom?

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:44.800
Well, all I know is that she was female.

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:46.670
How pathetic.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:48.640
Are you telling me that you
couldn't protect one woman?

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:53.440
Still no good. It's still no good.

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:58.180
Unless we make things stricter,
Kozue will be hurt again.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:02.050
Kozue will... KOZUE WILL! Damn!

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:04.650
Damn! Damn!
Damn! Damn!

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:06.450
- Damn!
- Ikumi...!

00:16:12.670 --> 00:16:13.670
There!

00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:15.130
- Wow! So cute!
- Congratulations!

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:17.000
This is my present to you, Pat.

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:19.870
It's a Ralph Lawrence quality handkerchief.

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:21.670
What a great present, Pat!

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:23.480
I don't want it!

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:24.840
I want Juli's.

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:28.110
But this...!

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:30.770
Why that's...
What are you doing with that?

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:35.010
You know about the backup battery, right?

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:38.720
Kouji's awfully late.

00:16:45.630 --> 00:16:48.620
I apologize, Kouji. But rest assured.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:52.210
I'll find the person that assaulted her...

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:54.510
...and I will make sure they never,
ever try something like that again.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:56.770
You're missing the point!
I want you to change the system!

00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:58.910
Your method is wrong!

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:02.750
- Wrong?
- Yeah.

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:05.310
Are you saying that I'd make a mistake?

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:10.620
I'm not mistaken!
I will never make another mistake!

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:12.750
Ikumi. Change the system.

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:15.120
There you go with your
carefree comments!

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:17.830
You're telling me to return things to how
they were after what happened to Kozue?

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:20.230
How could you say such
a thing in front of me?

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:22.070
Ikumi...!

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:24.800
Who are you to show off? You, who can't
protect Aoi, just one person!

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:26.300
What have you done to protect her?

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:32.080
I've succeeded in shutting up the fools
aboard the Ryvius! That in turn protects Aoi!

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:36.580
If she's important to you, shouldn't you be
by her side? Isn't that true?

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:39.290
Fundamentally, that doesn't
serve as a solution!

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:41.580
Not from you,
who's crazy about another girl!

00:17:42.060 --> 00:17:43.420
It's over between us!

00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:51.590
<i>Right now, I'm by Aoi's side.</i>
<i>I want to protect her.</i>

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:57.640
What the hell's that supposed to mean?

00:17:58.170 --> 00:18:01.140
What do you mean, "protect her"?
It's too late! It's too late!

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:03.570
It's too late! It's too late!

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:08.570
Stop basing your opinions
on what you want to believe!

00:18:09.680 --> 00:18:10.650
Kouji!

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:14.220
Why that's... the gun Blue had.

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:32.600
- What's the matter?
- That's Aoi's voice!

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:37.210
So you're the reason we
could not find Airs Blue.

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:40.680
This is an act of betrayal
against everyone aboard this ship.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.540
No! I only helped Blue.

00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:49.040
Kouji. Why didn't you report that?
What's wrong with you?

00:18:49.720 --> 00:18:51.420
Do you have to be that much
of a good buddy to everyone?

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:55.620
Can't you... Can't you at least feel a little
of the suffering we're going through?

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:58.160
That's the kinda guy he is!

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:00.490
No! I just want this current system to...!

00:19:00.670 --> 00:19:02.000
Shut up!

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:17.710
Ikumi...!

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:20.720
Your actions are at direct
odds with this system.

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:22.850
Please. Listen to me.

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:26.580
Then change the Ryvius!
Right now! Do it right away!

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:29.660
Sorry. I don't know how.

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:32.330
But I'm sure of one thing.

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:35.170
The methods currently used...!

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:38.760
The methods currently used won't please her.
Aren't I right, Ikumi?

00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:43.000
There's no way Kozue
would be pleased with it!

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:46.500
KOUJI!

00:19:55.490 --> 00:19:57.460
Yeah, it's me.

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:02.320
Oh, Kevin? I see.
All right, I'll be right there.

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:11.660
<i>Kouji. You're unable to part with Aoi...</i>

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:14.800
<i>... part with your past</i>

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:19.640
I believed that you were different.
That's why I...!

00:20:20.380 --> 00:20:23.310
- Let go! Let go!
- Stop fussing!

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:26.890
How could you do such a thing?

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:30.050
It's all for Faina! You're an obstacle
as far as Faina is concerned!

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:33.050
What are you saying? What?

00:20:40.430 --> 00:20:42.160
Are you in pain, Kouji?

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:50.070
Kouji. Why won't you understand?

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:52.070
Why, Kouji?

00:20:54.050 --> 00:20:56.210
We can't proceed to the future
until we cut off our past.

00:20:56.720 --> 00:20:58.580
Why can't you understand that?

00:21:01.550 --> 00:21:05.320
<i>We must sever the bothersome past,</i>
<i>in order to fully live today.</i>

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:13.000
I will follow Ikumi. Yes.

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:15.960
I will never become your past.

00:21:16.740 --> 00:21:18.800
You will become my past.

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:25.040
I can understand your desire to start over.

00:21:34.390 --> 00:21:38.760
But isn't one's past important in
order for one to continue living.

00:21:40.490 --> 00:21:41.860
<i>It's all your fault.</i>

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:47.320
<i>Because you tried to tell others that</i>
<i>I violated the teachings of Arne.</i>

00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:50.170
<i>Yes. You too.</i>

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:52.770
It's senseless.

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:55.240
No matter how you try to negate
the existence of others.

00:21:56.910 --> 00:21:58.070
You cannot erase...

00:21:58.780 --> 00:22:00.250
...your past.

00:22:07.410 --> 00:22:11.680
In your dry eyes...

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:16.750
...a silhouette appears

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:21.450
The blue colored future...

00:22:21.450 --> 00:22:28.190
...swayed and glittered

00:22:29.360 --> 00:22:37.600
Ah... No one wants...

00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:46.210
...freedom out of pity

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:54.650
Ah... To the days I feared...

00:22:54.650 --> 00:22:58.560
...that I'd end up hurting someone,

00:22:58.560 --> 00:23:04.930
goodbye

00:23:08.920 --> 00:23:09.820
Infinite Ryvius

00:23:09.820 --> 00:23:11.790
Infinite Ryvius
Next episode: Kouji Aiba
Kouji, whom I've known
since we were little.

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:12.920
Infinite Ryvius
Next episode: Kouji Aiba
Kouji, who's earnest.

00:23:12.920 --> 00:23:13.590
Next episode: Kouji Aiba

00:23:13.590 --> 00:23:15.590
Next episode: Kouji Aiba
Kouji, who shows off.

00:23:15.590 --> 00:23:17.830
Next episode: Kouji Aiba
Kouji, who's quick to sulk.

00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:21.600
Next episode: Kouji Aiba
My... Kouji Aiba...!

00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:25.740
Next episode: Kouji Aiba
Kouji. Kouji!

00:23:25.740 --> 00:23:29.070
Next episode: Kouji Aiba
I love you! I could die for you!
